From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:07:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: Serve the USB of a DP Alt Mode partner on
 T8132

T8132 runs no DisplayPort-only lanes, and DisplayPort beside USB3 only
with its usb3-dp calibration, which the J713 tree does not carry. A
partner that enters DP Alt Mode, such as a USB-C hub with a video port,
made atcphy_mux_check() refuse the mode with -ENODEV. By then tipd had
already taken the USB role down for the change, so the hub that had just
enumerated over USB2 disappeared, and the retries failed the same way:

  sn201202x 1-0a: failed to configure Type-C connection: -19
  sn201202x 1-0a: cable revalidation failed after 3 attempts

DP Alt Mode keeps the partner's USB on the other wires: USB2 next to
four DP lanes (pin assignments C and E), USB3 next to two (D). On T8132,
ask the PHY for that USB instead of the DisplayPort it cannot run: USB2
for C and E, and USB3 for D without the usb3-dp calibration, which the
USB2-only downgrade below still takes to USB2 when SuperSpeed is off.

Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 04f2c7dff748dca2d6ddde4a08ea75cd1ebf2bc0)
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc-test.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c      | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc-test.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc-test.c
index a26d8d4c49..79ecc338ad 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc-test.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc-test.c
@@ -87,6 +87,18 @@ static void atcphy_test_target_mode_t8132(struct kunit *test)
 	state.alt = &dp;
 	state.mode = TYPEC_DP_STATE_D;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atcphy_typec_target_mode(atcphy, &state), APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB2);
+	/* No DisplayPort-only lanes: the USB2 beside them still runs. */
+	state.mode = TYPEC_DP_STATE_C;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atcphy_typec_target_mode(atcphy, &state), APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB2);
+	state.mode = TYPEC_DP_STATE_E;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atcphy_typec_target_mode(atcphy, &state), APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB2);
+	/* SuperSpeed without the DP calibration: pin assignment D runs USB3. */
+	atcphy->t8132_ss = true;
+	atcphy->ss_tunables = true;
+	state.mode = TYPEC_DP_STATE_D;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atcphy_typec_target_mode(atcphy, &state), APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB3);
+	state.mode = TYPEC_DP_STATE_C;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atcphy_typec_target_mode(atcphy, &state), APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB2);
 	state.alt = NULL;
 	state.mode = TYPEC_STATE_SAFE;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, atcphy_typec_target_mode(atcphy, &state), APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_OFF);
diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index 4ad4355b8e..3e588853bc 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -5343,6 +5343,27 @@ static enum atcphy_mode atcphy_typec_target_mode(struct apple_atcphy *atcphy,
 	if (atcphy->fixed_usb2 && target_mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_OFF)
 		target_mode = APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB2;
 
+	/*
+	 * T8132 runs no DisplayPort-only lanes, and DisplayPort beside USB3
+	 * only with its calibration. A partner that enters DP Alt Mode keeps
+	 * its USB on the other wires: USB2 next to four DP lanes (pin
+	 * assignments C and E), USB3 next to two (D). Serve that USB rather
+	 * than refuse the mode, which would leave the port without USB at all.
+	 */
+	if (atcphy->hw->gen == ATCPHY_GENERATION_T8132) {
+		enum atcphy_mode usb_mode = target_mode;
+
+		if (target_mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_DP)
+			usb_mode = APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB2;
+		else if (target_mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB3_DP && !atcphy->tunables.usb3_dp)
+			usb_mode = APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB3;
+		if (usb_mode != target_mode) {
+			dev_warn(atcphy->dev,
+				 "DisplayPort is not available on this port: serving its USB only\n");
+			target_mode = usb_mode;
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (atcphy->hw->usb2_only &&
 	    (!atcphy->t8132_ss || !atcphy->ss_tunables) &&
 	    (target_mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB3 || target_mode == APPLE_ATCPHY_MODE_USB3_DP))
